<title>FRANCE: Fr.Telecom union calls strike for June 10.</title>
<headline>Fr.Telecom union calls strike for June 10.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The CGT union called on Tuesday for a one-day strike and a demonstration in Paris on June 10 to protest against a planned partial privatisation.</p>
<p>The CGT said in a statement it has called for the stoppage with employees of the state-owned La Poste and other organisations. It called for pay increases and shorter working hours, and for France Telecom to remain in state hands to ensure a full, modern public service.</p>
<p>Telecommunications Minister Francois Fillon has said the state must sell 30-35 percent of France Telecom as other European operators are being privatised and if the government continued to hold all the capital this would endanger its international alliances.</p>
</text>
